re\",\n    \"result.best_correct_score\",\n    \"result.improvement_001\",\n    \"result.improvement_002\",\n    \"result.improvement_003\",\n    \"result.top_program_01\",\n    \"result.top_program_02\",\n    \"result.top_program_03\",\n    \"result.total_attempts\",\n    \"result.total_correct_programs\",\n    \"result.total_evaluated_programs\",\n    \"result.total_ideas\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"nl -ba paper.tex | sed -n '235,247p;277,348p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"nl -ba paper.tex | sed -n '235,247p;277,348p'\"","aggregated_output":"   235\t\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/component_comparison.pdf}\n   236\t\\caption{Matched component comparisons on development data only. Left: forest computation with and without the exact leaf-game component. Right: logistic computation with and without integration. Each category shows the two recorded seed values and a mean tick; the vertical axis is restricted to $[0.8,1]$. Ger/ACS denote dataset and labels underneath give coalition caps. The unchanged model family is retained in each comparison; structural access and work still differ.}\n   237\t\\label{fig:components}\n   238\t% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/all_programs]]\n   239\t\\end{figure}\n   240\t\n   241\tDevelopment comparisons in Figure~\\ref{fig:components} support family-localized changes. At cap 64, German forest reference agreement changes from 0.858--0.870 without the leaf-game component to 0.9924--0.9929 with it. German logistic changes from 0.946--0.951 without integration to approximately 0.9963 with integration. In both ACS comparisons, the structure-aware outputs agree with exhaustive references to the displayed precision. These are matched configuration comparisons, not evidence that an untested safeguard or formula alone caused every gain.\n   242\t% @evidence[[analysis_summary.json#/development]]\n   243\t\n   244\tThe sampled development estimates also show nonmonotone cap behavior: ACS forest mean agreement without its structure component falls from approximately 0.9674 at cap 64 to 0.9512 at cap 256. German logistic without integration similarly falls from about 0.9488 to 0.9137. This concerns the custom sampled fallback, not the final library curve. More sampled coalitions need not improve an individual finite estimate, and the recorded comparisons do not isolate whether sampling mix, fit conditioning, or another interaction explains the pattern. No missing ablation is treated as a measured failure.\n   245\t% @evidence[[analysis_summary.json#/development]]\n   246\t\n   247\t\\section{Discussion and Limitations}\n   277\tThe acquisition hashes normalized raw predictor content before population filtering, splitting, or preprocessing. Numeric fields use canonical finite decimal strings, categorical fields use Unicode normalization and normalized whitespace, and missing values have a typed sentinel. Predictor hashes exclude identifiers and labels. German content groups are split between development and final data, then deterministically partitioned into training, validation, and explanation subsets. All California/New York predictor-content overlaps are removed before ACS content groups are selected. Such exclusion changes population composition and does not substitute for population weighting.\n   278\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L41-L155]]\n   279\t\n   280\tACS uses \\texttt{AGEP, COW, SCHL, MAR, OCCP, POBP, RELSHIPP, WKHP, SEX, RAC1P}. The acquisition retains the adult income population restriction and the binary \\texttt{PINCP>50000} target. Native \\texttt{RELSHIPP} is used without inventing a crosswalk to the absent \\texttt{RELP}. German positive labels correspond to the original code 2. These target conventions matter when interpreting attribution signs; a positive value raises the serialized model's chosen positive-class probability, not an abstract notion of benefit.\n   281\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L151]]\n   282\t\n   283\tTraining vocabularies map sorted categorical values to integer codes, with unseen values mapped to $-1$. Numeric imputation and all scaling statistics are training-fitted. The serialized predictor is checked against the fitted estimator on queries and background before explanation. This is a finite probe check, not proof of equivalent behavior on every hybrid input. Final validation accuracies are 0.67 for German logistic, 0.65--0.69 for German forests, approximately 0.7609 for ACS logistic and 0.7755--0.7773 for ACS forests. Logistic fits report convergence with 19 iterations on German and 13 on ACS. These diagnostics characterize the explained predictors; the attribution study does not establish predictive adequacy.\n   284\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718]]\n   285\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L838-L847]]\n   286\t% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n   287\t\n   288\t\\subsection{Structure-Aware Computation and Numerical Safeguards}\n   289\t\\paragraph{Leaf contributions.}\n   290\tFor a viable leaf, the expected indicator under independent feature inclusion with probability $t$ is $t^p(1-t)^q$. Including a required-positive feature changes this by $t^{p-1}(1-t)^q$, while including a required-negative feature changes it by $-t^p(1-t)^{q-1}$. Integrating each marginal from zero to one yields Equation~\\ref{eq:leaf}. Features not constrained by that leaf contribute zero. A constant leaf contributes no feature attribution, though it contributes to the empty/full value. Repeated splits are intersected into lower-exclusive and upper-inclusive bounds; contradictory paths are removed. The exact finite-game claim depends on matching these traversal semantics.\n   291\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/forest.py#L11-L81]]\n   292\t\n   293\t\\paragraph{Frequency truncation is not discretization certification.}\n   294\tIn Equation~\\ref{eq:logistic}, the phase difference has magnitude at most two and every inclusion factor has magnitude at most one. Thus the omitted tail beyond frequency $W$ is bounded coordinatewise by\n   295\t\\begin{equation}\n   296\t 2\\int_W^\\infty\\frac{d\\omega}{\\sinh(\\pi\\omega)}\n   297\t =-\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\log\\tanh\\!\\left(\\frac{\\pi W}{2}\\right).\n   298\t\\end{equation}\n   299\tThis is the source implementation's frequency-tail bound. It does not bound mesh discretization error on the retained interval. The implementation uses agreement under refinement and endpoint conservation as additional numerical diagnostics, rejects nonfinite arithmetic or excessive phase ranges, and averages all background rows only after successful integration. Prefix/suffix products keep zero mixture factors well-defined. The wrapper catches floating-point overflow and invalid arithmetic and returns rejection without consuming the sampling generator.\n   300\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L12-L140]]\n   301\t\n   302\t\\paragraph{Fallback safeguards.}\n   303\tIndependent permutation paths provide bounded marginal observations in $[-1,1]$. For $m$ complete paths, coordinate sample variance $s_j^2$, and $\\alpha=0.05$, the implemented simultaneous radius is\n   304\t\\begin{equation}\n   305\t r_j=\\sqrt{\\frac{2s_j^2\\log(4d/\\alpha)}{m}}\n   306\t       +\\frac{14\\log(4d/\\alpha)}{3(m-1)}.\n   307\t\\end{equation}\n   308\tIt is used only when at least two complete paths exist. The path estimate is selected only when absolute-value intervals strictly separate selected from excluded features and the selected signs exclude zero. Otherwise regression is retained. Even if the underlying bound's conditions hold, this is not a guarantee conditional on selection and supplies no observed certification rate here. Permutation paths, not individual within-path marginals, are independent sampling units. Endpoint-constrained regression is not covered by that path-bound calculation.\n   309\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/reliability.py#L66-L161]]\n   310\t\n   311\t\\paragraph{Implementation evidence.}\n   312\tReadable files in \\texttt{source\\_evidence/selected/} contain dispatch, integration, forest calculation, and the attribution-only response interface. The corresponding development snapshots are in \\texttt{source\\_evidence/sampled/} and \\texttt{source\\_evidence/forest/}. The release includes independent small-tree and logistic validation routines, but there is no recorded execution of those routines in the retained research evidence. They are not additional controls, replications, or measured ablations. Provenance hashes identify artifacts; the equations above are supported by the readable source, not merely by a prior audit verdict.\n   313\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/validate_forest.py]]\n   314\t% @evidence[[source_evidence/selected/validate_logistic_fourier.py]]\n   315\t\n   316\tConcrete source anchors are \\path{source_evidence/selected/forest.py:11} for path intersections and leaf contributions,\n   317\t\\path{source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py:12} for the numerical integrand and refinements,\n   318\tand \\path{source_evidence/selected/reliability.py:163} for dispatch. Metric definitions are in\n   319\t\\path{source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py:1014}.\n   320\t\n   321\t\\subsection{Episode-Level Reliability and Reference Uncertainty}\n   322\tTable~\\ref{tab:extended} lists every final non-replay condition and cap. Means within each row average the fixed query set and, for structure-aware outputs, repeated calls. No new evaluation is run to create this table. Table~\\ref{tab:intervals} preserves the stored query-bootstrap intervals, averaged over caps and repeated calls as specified in the main text. They must not be read as uncertainty for the difference between two methods.\n   323\t% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n   324\t\n   325\t\\begin{longtable}{llrrrr}\n   326\t\\caption{Final seed/condition/cap reference agreement. Display precision can hide residual error near one.}\\label{tab:extended}\\\\\n   327\t\\toprule Seed & Condition & Cap & One-shot & Split cap & Structure\\\\\\midrule\n   328\t\\endfirsthead\n   329\t\\toprule Seed & Condition & Cap & One-shot & Split cap & Structure\\\\\\midrule\n   330\t\\endhead\n   331\t% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n   332\t104729 & German / logistic & 64 & 0.9292 & 0.3134 & 0.9967 \\\\\n   333\t104729 & German / logistic & 256 & 0.9754 & 0.9713 & 0.9967 \\\\\n   334\t104729 & German / logistic & 1024 & 0.9894 & 0.9893 & 0.9967 \\\\\n   335\t104729 & German / forest & 64 & 0.8836 & 0.2904 & 0.9937 \\\\\n   336\t104729 & German / forest & 256 & 0.9547 & 0.9454 & 0.9937 \\\\\n   337\t104729 & German / forest & 1024 & 0.9806 & 0.9777 & 0.9937 \\\\\n   338\t104729 & ACS / logistic & 64 & 0.9604 & 0.9363 & 1.0000 \\\\\n   339\t104729 & ACS / logistic & 256 & 0.9834 & 0.9804 & 1.0000 \\\\\n   340\t104729 & ACS / logistic & 1024 & 1.0000 & 0.9936 & 1.0000 \\\\\n   341\t104729 & ACS / forest & 64 & 0.9604 & 0.9348 & 1.0000 \\\\\n   342\t104729 & ACS / forest & 256 & 0.9853 & 0.9843 & 1.0000 \\\\\n   343\t104729 & ACS / forest & 1024 & 1.0000 & 0.9942 & 1.0000 \\\\\n   344\t130363 & German / logistic & 64 & 0.9361 & 0.3912 & 0.9966 \\\\\n   345\t130363 & German / logistic & 256 & 0.9764 & 0.9670 & 0.9966 \\\\\n   346\t130363 & German / logistic & 1024 & 0.9880 & 0.9889 & 0.9966 \\\\\n   347\t130363 & German / forest & 64 & 0.8689 & 0.2905 & 0.9935 \\\\\n   348\t130363 & German / forest & 256 & 0.9567 & 0.9421 & 0.9935 \\\\\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
