wall seconds, rounded to 700.37, including references, comparators, training and overhead; candidate-only latency is unavailable.\n sources: final.metric.wall_seconds refs: source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1310-L1343,paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/wall_seconds\n7: Four final dataset/model conditions are German logistic, German forest, ACS logistic and ACS forest; no additional task list or downstream study is present.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\n8: Final seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921; caps 64/256/1024; six repeats per cap; sixteen fixed queries and training-background rows per fitted condition.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L34-L36,source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1316-L1319,paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\n9: Final German retained splits are 300/100/100 records and twenty groups; ACS 20000/6667/6667 and ten groups. These are protocol counts, not independent explained-sample counts.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L61-L155,source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json,source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718\n10: German uses original class code 2. ACS uses 2024 PUMS, native RELSHIPP without a RELP crosswalk, the retained adult filter and PINCP>50000 target.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L155,source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json\n11: German development/final content groups are disjoint. ACS uses California development and New York final data after excluding raw predictor-content overlaps.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L155,source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json\n12: Training-fitted ordinal vocabularies use unseen code -1; numeric medians and standardization are training fitted; queries/background use fixed ordering.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718,source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L838-L842\n13: Logistic regression uses lbfgs, max_iter 500 and tolerance 1e-7. Forests use sixty-four trees, depth six and n_jobs one.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L833-L837\n14: ACS references enumerate ten-feature finite games; German references average two independent cap-4096 library estimates. Their half-difference is a proxy, not a calibrated interval.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L774-L796,source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L849-L858\n15: Stored 95-percent intervals use 1000 bootstrap resamples of sixteen query-level means after cap/repeat averaging, conditional on one fitted model/reference.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1154-L1159\n16: The normalized L1 agreement floor is 0.001; signs at magnitude at most 1e-8 are zero; top-three ties follow coordinate order. Endpoint residual is capped at one.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1014-L1030\n17: Library KernelExplainer uses identity link, l1_reg zero and nsamples equal to cap. Two independent split-cap calls each use floor(cap/2).\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L757-L772,source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L860-L868\n18: Forest attribution uses signed leaf-game beta-integral coefficients over all trees/background rows, intersecting repeated splits and retaining float32 predictor-input semantics.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/selected/forest.py#L11-L81,source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L720-L755\n19: Probability-scale logistic integration uses ceil(d/2) inclusion nodes, eight-node frequency panels, cutoff eight and at most 2048 frequency nodes; tail tolerance 1e-10 and mesh/efficiency tolerances 1e-8.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L12-L140\n20: Two consecutive mesh agreements are required. Failure for any background row rejects integration; frequency-tail control is not a rigorous discretization bound.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L43-L140\n21: Dispatch uses forest structure directly, then generic enumeration when cap covers 2^d-2 nontrivial coalitions before logistic integration; branch counts are unrecorded.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/selected/reliability.py#L163-L197\n22: The sampled fallback combines independent complete paths and importance-corrected constrained regression. Alpha 0.05 separation is used only with at least two paths; acceptance coverage is absent.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/selected/reliability.py#L66-L197\n23: The release contains independent validation routines without retained executions. They are not additional empirical controls.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/selected/validate_forest.py,source_evidence/selected/validate_logistic_fourier.py\n24: Recorded dependencies include NumPy 2.1.3, SciPy 1.15.3, scikit-learn 1.6.1, SHAP 0.48.0, pandas 2.2.3 and folktables 0.0.12; a fresh full-lock installation was not tested.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt\n25: German reference mean absolute coordinate half-differences are about 1.05e-4 logistic and 1.20e-4 forest; no error decomposition follows.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: analysis_summary.json#/reference_uncertainty\n26: Seed-104729 query-bootstrap intervals round to [0.99618,0.99709] German logistic and [0.99292,0.99442] German forest.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/0/observations/fidelity_instance_bootstrap_ci95,paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/solution/cases/1/observations/fidelity_instance_bootstrap_ci95\n27: Final cap-64 structure agreement is 0.9966/0.9937 German logistic/forest, versus library 0.9347/0.8806; ACS structure rounds to one versus library 0.9577/0.9636.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: analysis_summary.json#/final\n28: At cap 1024 final library means are 0.9889/0.9802 German logistic/forest and round to one for both ACS cases. This does not establish necessity of structure-aware access.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: analysis_summary.json#/final\n29: Split-cap German means at cap 64 are 0.3341/0.2995, recovering to 0.9699/0.9448 at cap 256; recorded diagnostics do not isolate a cause.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: analysis_summary.json#/final\n30: Final validation accuracy is 0.67 German logistic, 0.65--0.69 German forest, about 0.7609 ACS logistic and 0.7755--0.7773 ACS forest. Converged logistic fits use 19 and 13 iterations respectively.\n sources: final.evidence.episodes refs: paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\n31: Development uses seeds 1729/2718, eight queries, four repeated calls, caps 64/256; comparisons are supporting evidence, not held-out confirmation.\n sources: result.top_program_01,result.top_program_02,result.top_program_03 refs: paper_data.json#/all_programs,source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate.py#L1316-L1319\n32: German cap-64 forest agreement changes from 0.858--0.870 to 0.9924--0.9929 with leaf computation; logistic from 0.946--0.951 to about 0.9963 with integration.\n sources: result.top_program_01,result.top_program_02,result.top_program_03 refs: analysis_summary.json#/development\n33: Custom sampled development means are nonmonotone from cap 64 to 256: ACS forest about 0.9674 to 0.9512 and German logistic 0.9488 to 0.9137; no unique cause is established.\n sources: result.top_program_01,result.top_program_02,result.top_program_03 refs: analysis_summary.json#/development\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
