s equal one; these are separate assessments.\",\n105:      \"claim\": \"Stored vectors have zero maximum coordinate range across repeats within each fixed cap/model/query.\",\n116:      \"claim\": \"Pure reference sign agreement is 0.9994791667, not the mixed evaluator sign metric.\",\n119:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1038-L1053\"\n129:      \"claim\": \"Mean normalized endpoint residual is 1.27919753412707e-11, control pass rate one, failed-call fraction zero and replay error zero.\",\n137:        \"final.metric.failed_fraction\",\n143:      \"claim\": \"The recorded full workload takes 700.3707705293782 wall seconds, rounded to 700.37, including references, comparators, training and overhead; candidate-only latency is unavailable.\",\n145:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1310-L1343\",\n155:      \"claim\": \"Four final dataset/model conditions are German logistic, German forest, ACS logistic and ACS forest; no additional task list or downstream study is present.\",\n166:      \"claim\": \"Final seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921; caps 64/256/1024; six repeats per cap; sixteen fixed queries and training-background rows per fitted condition.\",\n168:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L34-L36\",\n169:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1316-L1319\",\n179:      \"claim\": \"Final German retained splits are 300/100/100 records and twenty groups; ACS 20000/6667/6667 and ten groups. These are protocol counts, not independent explained-sample counts.\",\n181:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L61-L155\",\n182:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json\",\n183:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718\"\n192:      \"claim\": \"German uses original class code 2. ACS uses 2024 PUMS, native RELSHIPP without a RELP crosswalk, the retained adult filter and PINCP>50000 target.\",\n194:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L155\",\n195:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json\"\n204:      \"claim\": \"German development/final content groups are disjoint. ACS uses California development and New York final data after excluding raw predictor-content overlaps.\",\n206:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/capture.py#L72-L155\",\n207:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/data_provenance.json\"\n216:      \"claim\": \"Training-fitted ordinal vocabularies use unseen code -1; numeric medians and standardization are training fitted; queries/background use fixed ordering.\",\n218:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L687-L718\",\n219:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L838-L842\"\n228:      \"claim\": \"Logistic regression uses lbfgs, max_iter 500 and tolerance 1e-7. Forests use sixty-four trees, depth six and n_jobs one.\",\n230:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L833-L837\"\n239:      \"claim\": \"ACS references enumerate ten-feature finite games; German references average two independent cap-4096 library estimates. Their half-difference is a proxy, not a calibrated interval.\",\n241:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L774-L796\",\n242:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L849-L858\"\n251:      \"claim\": \"Stored 95-percent intervals use 1000 bootstrap resamples of sixteen query-level means after cap/repeat averaging, conditional on one fitted model/reference.\",\n253:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1154-L1159\"\n262:      \"claim\": \"The normalized L1 agreement floor is 0.001; signs at magnitude at most 1e-8 are zero; top-three ties follow coordinate order. Endpoint residual is capped at one.\",\n264:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L1014-L1030\"\n273:      \"claim\": \"Library KernelExplainer uses identity link, l1_reg zero and nsamples equal to cap. Two independent split-cap calls each use floor(cap/2).\",\n275:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L757-L772\",\n276:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L860-L868\"\n285:      \"claim\": \"Forest attribution uses signed leaf-game beta-integral coefficients over all trees/background rows, intersecting repeated splits and retaining float32 predictor-input semantics.\",\n287:        \"source_evidence/selected/forest.py#L11-L81\",\n288:        \"source_evidence/evaluation/evaluate_final.py#L720-L755\"\n297:      \"claim\": \"Probability-scale logistic integration uses ceil(d/2) inclusion nodes, eight-node frequency panels, cutoff eight and at most 2048 frequency nodes; tail tolerance 1e-10 and mesh/efficiency tolerances 1e-8.\",\n299:        \"source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L12-L140\"\n308:      \"claim\": \"Two consecutive mesh agreements are required. Failure for any background row rejects integration; frequency-tail control is not a rigorous discretization bound.\",\n310:        \"source_evidence/selected/logistic_fourier.py#L43-L140\"\n319:      \"claim\": \"Dispatch uses forest structure directly, then generic enumeration when cap covers 2^d-2 nontrivial coalitions before logistic integration; branch counts are unrecorded.\",\n321:        \"source_evidence/selected/reliability.py#L163-L197\"\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"claim_count\": 143,\n  \"evidence_validation\": {\n    \"anchored_references\": 90,\n    \"dangling_references\": 0,\n    \"manifests_checked\": 16,\n    \"resolved_references\": 112,\n    \"total_references\": 202\n  }\n}\n\\path{source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt}. The numerical stack includes NumPy 2.1.3 \\citep{Harris2020}, SciPy 1.15.3 \\citep{Virtanen2020}, scikit-learn 1.6.1 \\citep{Pedregosa2011}, SHAP 0.48.0, pandas 2.2.3 \\citep{McKinney2010}, and folktables 0.0.12. These are the recorded requirements, not a claim that every dependency was independently reinstalled during writing. Figure rendering uses Matplotlib \\citep{Hunter2007}; writing-time rendering tools are isolated outside the manuscript workspace.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt]]\n\n\\texttt{REPRODUCIBILITY.md} records offline evaluation and data-recapture commands, source locations, and rendering steps. To regenerate quantitative figures and tables from the retained registry, run \\texttt{python build\\_artifacts.py} in an environment with NumPy, Matplotlib, and Pillow. This script generates Figures~\\ref{fig:final}, \\ref{fig:components}, and \\ref{fig:reference}, and all numerical table fragments. It does not rerun training or explanations. Figure~\\ref{fig:overview} is a separate conceptual rendering; its placeholder is self-guarded and is not an experimental result. Adjacent provenance sidecars link derived artifacts to retained episode arrays.\n\nThe final evaluation's 700.37-second wall total includes references, library comparators, training, and execution overhead; it is not per-query latency or CPU usage. The study does not have an equal-wall-time or total-model-evaluation benchmark for structure-aware computation. Reference prediction-row counters and baseline timings are present in the retained observations, but do not recover a complete candidate cost ledger. The stated source-task CPU allowance is not measured consumption and is not reported as such.\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/wall_seconds]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n\n\\subsection{LLM Usage}\nLLM-based assistants were used for research design proposals, estimator code preparation, inspection of source and evaluation artifacts, reference-query planning, manuscript framing and drafting, derivation of descriptive tables and plotting code, and grounding/format checks. The retained evaluations were executed by the evaluation workflow, not by prose generation. Written independent validation routines without recorded executions are explicitly distinguished from measured evidence. No human-subject judgments, human review outcomes, or manual verification by domain experts are claimed. Literature use here is limited to directly retrieved known primary bibliographic records and available abstracts; no citation-network traversal or search for the prohibited study was used in manuscript preparation. Reference discovery noise was removed rather than treated as read or relevant literature.\n\n\\end{document}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
